1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:04,774
If you want her, you'll have to use
your dual blades to take her from us.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:08,637
If you can defeat me in combat,
you'll be free to take Asuna.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:13,700
On the other hand, if you lose, you
will join the Knights of the Blood Oath.

4
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:18,730
Yeah, okay.

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:21,857
If you want to settle this
with swords, that's fine by me.

6
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,881
We'll have ourselves a duel then.

7
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:28,180
Better hurry, folks!

8
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:31,040
The good seats are going fast! Who's next?

9
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:32,280
My god!

10
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,835
You're such an idiot!

11
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:35,477
How could you agree to a duel?

12
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:37,360
Okay, calm down. I'm sorry.

13
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,209
It's not like you gave
me any other choice.

14
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,660
The other day, when you used
your duel wielding skill,

15
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:46,391
I've never seen anything like that before.

16
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:49,597
Thing is, the commander has
his own unique skill, too.

17
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,617
I know I've seen it a bunch
of times myself the divine

18
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:57,477
blade it maximizes his
offensive and defensive moves

19
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:00,597
his attack is strong but
his defense is incredible

20
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:03,677
no one's ever seen the
commander's HP bar dipped down

21
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:07,697
into the yellow zone before
his invincibility is way

22
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:12,597
beyond the normal game balance
I know what if you lose

23
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:16,317
I don't care if I don't get
my leave of absence I care

24
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:19,635
about you having to join the
Knights of the Blood Oath.

25
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,180
Well, I'm not planning on losing easily.

26
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:47,457
Don't they do that?

27
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:52,360
I'm so happy that you're a
girl that I'm not having.

28
00:01:54,540 --> 00:01:58,160
You're just very happy to know.

29
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:01,617
Oh, I don't mind.

30
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:02,530
This will die again.

31
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:03,443
Thank you for all of us.

32
00:02:03,526 --> 00:02:04,356
Here we go.

33
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:05,269
Yawn.

34
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,286
I'm sorry about this, Kirito.

35
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:06,177
I didn't think this
would be such a big deal.

36
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,090
This is crazy.

37
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,516
Maybe I can get a cut of the tickets?

38
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:11,370
No.

39
00:03:11,453 --> 00:03:14,457
But when we're finished, you'll become
an official member of the Guild.

40
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,775
I'll consider this your first mission.

41
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:55,900
His shield?

42
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,580
Your reaction time is very impressive.

43
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,275
Yeah, and your defense is impregnable.

44
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,277
Not yet!

45
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,360
Give it time!

46
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,020
Be careful.

47
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:54,720
Now's my chance!

48
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:04,800
Ugh!

49
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,550
Ah!

50
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:10,690
Ah!

51
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:11,650
Ah!

52
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:23,380
Rubber, Rubber, Rubber!

53
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,757
Uh, don't you guys have
uniforms that aren't so flashy?

54
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:43,037
Actually, that's one of
our less flashy ones.

55
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:44,717
You look great!

56
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:50,357
I'm in a guild,

57
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,617
I guess it's sort of my fault.

58
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:54,637
Isn't it no?

59
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:58,097
This is a good opportunity
as a solo player.

60
00:05:58,180 --> 00:05:59,592
I got as far as I could.

61
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,099
That makes me feel a little better.

62
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,040
Hey, Kirito?

63
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,300
Why do you avoid guilds?

64
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:09,600
And people?

65
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:12,302
I hope you don't mind my asking.

66
00:06:13,880 --> 00:06:14,710
I mean,

67
00:06:14,793 --> 00:06:18,877
it's not because you're a beta tester or
because you have unique skills, is it?

68
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:20,560
You do care about people.

69
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:29,977
It was a long time ago,
about a year or so,

70
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:33,440
up to now, that was the
only guild I was in.

71
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:38,417
It was small, including me;
there were six of us in it.

72
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,580
They called themselves
the Moonlit Black Cats.

73
00:06:42,280 --> 00:06:46,377
As players, they were good, but their
levels were way lower than mine,

74
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,320
and I thought if I told them?

75
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:51,737
what my level was, they
wouldn't have wanted me around.

76
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:54,173
So I decided to keep my mouth shut about

77
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,517
it, and I joined up with them.

78
00:06:56,600 --> 00:07:00,800
I'd watch them, messing around,
having fun, and I guess I wanted

79
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:02,457
to be part of that too.

80
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,077
Then one day…

81
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:11,160
I'm

82
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:15,790
the

83
00:07:15,873 --> 00:07:16,703
reason

84
00:07:16,786 --> 00:07:17,616
the whole

85
00:07:17,699 --> 00:07:18,529
guild was wiped out.

86
00:07:18,612 --> 00:07:19,860
If I hadn't hidden the
fact that I was a beater,

87
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:23,866
I could have convinced them how
dangerous that trap really was.

88
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,420
I killed them.

89
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,010
Sachi.

90
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,260
All of them.

91
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:48,507
I'm not gonna die, got that?

92
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:52,517
I can't die because...

93
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,640
I have to protect you.

94
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:14,100
I got a train.

95
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,200
That's right.

96
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:18,898
You, me, and one other guy
are going to form a party.

97
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,377
Then, we're all going to go
clear the dungeon on this floor.

98
00:08:22,460 --> 00:08:23,700
Hold on, Godfrey.

99
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,497
Kirito and I are already in...

100
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:27,377
I can't do anything about it, ma 'am.

101
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:30,837
Besides, as second-in-command, you
know we can't ignore the rules.

102
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:32,617
If he's going to be joining us,

103
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,717
then it's my job as
commander of the front lines

104
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:37,177
to take the kid out and
evaluate his skills.

105
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:38,697
But that's ridiculous.

106
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:39,977
He doesn't need evaluation.

107
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,413
He's stronger than you.

108
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:45,597
Kid, in 30 minutes, I want to
see you at the Western Gate.

109
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:46,510
Hoorah!

110
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,780
We finally had a chance to be alone.

111
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:56,940
I'll be back soon.

112
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,669
Think you can wait for me?

113
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,030
Mm-hmm.

114
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:02,900
Just be careful.

115
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:10,190
Hey, kid!

116
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:11,635
We're waiting for ya!

117
00:09:17,860 --> 00:09:18,960
Are you serious?

118
00:09:19,840 --> 00:09:20,670
Yep.

119
00:09:20,753 --> 00:09:21,583
Look at it this way.

120
00:09:21,666 --> 00:09:22,597
We're all on the same guild,

121
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:26,856
so I figured now's a good time as
any for you guys to bury the hatchet.

122
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:36,037
about the other day i apologize for
my behavior i was rude to you and

123
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:42,617
i i promise it won't happen again
yeah sure all right ladies time to

124
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:48,297
focus today i'll be checking out how
you react to dangerous situations

125
00:09:48,380 --> 00:09:52,321
so i'm gonna need you to hand over
all the crystals in your storage

126
00:09:52,980 --> 00:09:55,960
Even my Teleport Crystals? Mm-hmm.

127
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:05,920
Yeah, okay.

128
00:10:10,040 --> 00:10:10,900
Awesome!

129
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:13,500
Now, let's go clear a dungeon!

130
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,110
Yay.

131
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:30,567
This looks like a good
place to take a break.

132
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,400
Ciao time, ladies.

133
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:43,960
Say ah!

134
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,880
We've been poisoned.

135
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:23,791
What the hell's going on?

136
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,380
You packed the water cura deal.

137
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:29,220
What'd you do, you bastard?

138
00:11:29,720 --> 00:11:31,300
Antidote crystals, hurry!

139
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,640
Poor, sad old Godfrey.

140
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:42,233
I always knew you were a colossal idiot,

141
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:45,401
but this proves you're
even dumber than I thought.

142
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:49,240
Don't do this!

143
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,280
No, stop it!

144
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,080
Here's my plan.

145
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:04,540
Our party was walking along when...

146
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:09,908
We were attacked by this gang of criminal
players who appeared out of nowhere.

147
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:13,259
You both fought hard, but
you were killed in battle.

148
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:15,540
It was just me against all of them.

149
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:19,700
And somehow, I courageously and
single-handedly fought them all off!

150
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,470
Huh?

151
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:28,920
Huh?

152
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:32,310
Uh!

153
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:39,960
Huh?

154
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:57,060
You know, I just killed an
innocent bystander because of you.

155
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:59,660
How am I going to live with myself?

156
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:03,768
From over here, you look like
you're having a blast doing it.

157
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:07,877
Why the hell would a guy like you
join the Knights of the Blood Oath?

158
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:10,877
You'd be more at home with
one of the criminal guilds.

159
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:12,880
What an interesting observation.

160
00:13:13,580 --> 00:13:15,180
You have sharp eyes.

161
00:13:16,660 --> 00:13:18,320
You're with Leafa and Coffin.

162
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:19,640
The murder guild.

163
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:25,289
That's where I got the skills
to paralyze bastards like you.

164
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:26,700
Where's my head?

165
00:13:27,060 --> 00:13:30,001
I better stop talking or
the poison will wear off.

166
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,649
And we wouldn't want that.

167
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,000
Time to finish you off for good.

168
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,640
The poison's not wearing off.

169
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,257
How's it feel? Come on.

170
00:13:49,340 --> 00:13:53,281
I want to know how it feels knowing
you're about to die like a dog.

171
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:54,510
What?

172
00:13:54,593 --> 00:13:56,560
Is your tongue paralyzed too?

173
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:03,000
Is this it?

174
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:06,600
Is this where I'm going to die?

175
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,120
Come on now!

176
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:10,874
It's your last chance to say something.

177
00:14:11,700 --> 00:14:13,600
You really are going to die.

178
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,300
Why do you keep struggling?

179
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,760
Are you afraid of dying after all?

180
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:45,840
No, I'm just not ready yet.

181
00:14:46,960 --> 00:14:48,400
Is that so?

182
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:51,600
That's the way I like it!

183
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,120
Die!

184
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:03,730
Die!

185
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:05,150
Die!

186
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,190
Heel!

187
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:24,640
I made it.

188
00:15:25,060 --> 00:15:26,780
I made it in time.

189
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:28,937
Thank God.

190
00:15:29,020 --> 00:15:30,280
I made it.

191
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:36,917
I was tracking your position
on the map the whole time,

192
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,980
and then I saw Godfrey disappear.

193
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:41,780
I got worried something happened.

194
00:15:42,800 --> 00:15:44,160
But you're alive.

195
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,080
I'm not dreaming, am I?

196
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:49,200
No, you're not.

197
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,180
Hang on.

198
00:15:54,660 --> 00:15:56,020
I'll finish this.

199
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:02,740
Asuna, I can explain everything.

200
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:06,509
We were just training when all
of a sudden there was this...

201
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:09,040
Damn you!

202
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:20,800
I give up. I surrender.

203
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,394
Please, don't kill me.

204
00:16:22,720 --> 00:16:23,877
I'll leave the guild.

205
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:25,777
You'll never see me again, I promise.

206
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,690
Please!

207
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,280
I don't want to die!

208
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:44,400
The oldest trick in the book,
and you fell for it, bitch!

209
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:04,860
Goddamn you, you murdered me.

210
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:25,480
I'm sorry.

211
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:29,920
This was all my fault, wasn't it?

212
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,100
Asuna.

213
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:39,580
I'm sorry.

214
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,597
But I...

215
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:45,440
I should stay away from you.

216
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,220
For your sake.

217
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,740
Asuna, my life belongs to you.

218
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:14,560
I'll give it up for you.

219
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,240
I want to stay with you until the end.

220
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:23,637
And I promise, I'll do anything
to protect you two. Forever.

221
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,920
No matter what.

222
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:26,460
I swear.

223
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:31,780
I'll do everything I can to make
sure you get back to the real world.

224
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:38,920
Asuna, could I stay
with you for the night?

225
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:00,820
Okay.

226
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:26,680
Don't look.

227
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:28,860
Not yet, anyway.

228
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,991
What are you waiting for?

229
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:34,910
Get undressed.

230
00:19:35,580 --> 00:19:36,815
Don't just sit there.

231
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,280
It's embarrassing.

232
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,860
No, wait, I didn't...

233
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:43,017
I mean, I just...

234
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:46,760
All I wanted was to spend the
night with you tonight and...

235
00:19:47,580 --> 00:19:49,720
Not the, uh, the other thing.

236
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:06,880
You, you, you dummy!

237
00:20:24,900 --> 00:20:27,160
Hey, what are you smiling about?

238
00:20:28,560 --> 00:20:32,900
I was just having a
dream about my old life.

239
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:35,360
It was weird.

240
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:39,600
And the dream I had,
everything in Aincrad,

241
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:43,617
everything that happened in
meeting you was just that, a dream.

242
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:45,000
And I was so scared.

243
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,660
But it wasn't.

244
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:48,540
Thank God it wasn't.

245
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:50,140
Now that sounds weird.

246
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:52,117
Don't you want to go back?

247
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:54,440
Of course I do. I do.

248
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:57,973
It's just, I don't want my
life here to disappear is all.

249
00:20:58,660 --> 00:21:01,484
The last two years have
been very special to me.

250
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,220
I realize that now.

251
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:08,860
Listen, Kirito.

252
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:14,140
I was thinking, maybe we could leave
the front lines for a while. What?

253
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,617
I'm scared.

254
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:22,637
I feel like if we return to the battlefield
now, something bad's gonna happen again.

255
00:21:22,720 --> 00:21:24,820
Or maybe I'm just tired of it all.

256
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,660
I know what you mean.

257
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:30,040
I guess I am too.

258
00:21:33,240 --> 00:21:35,420
In the southwest of Floor 22,

259
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:39,297
there's this tiny little
village by a lake and a forest.

260
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:44,297
First, we could get a
house together, and then...

261
00:21:44,380 --> 00:21:45,580
And then what?

262
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:51,780
Then we get married.

263
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:02,990
Okay.

264
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:20,117
I'm not so busy.

265
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:22,097
I heard too late.

266
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:26,460
The tune is a little bit.

267
00:22:28,880 --> 00:22:30,197
It's hard to even.

268
